kernel-collection-builder: KCB_TEXT_EXEC_ORDER=kernel-first keeps the pre-dyld-1378 __TEXT_EXEC order

dyld-1378 (macOS 26.5) started placing the kexts' __TEXT_EXEC segments before
the kernel's inside the collection's __TEXT_EXEC (stable_partition "kexts
first, static exe last"), so that xnu's __TEXT_BOOT_EXEC stays within branch
range of its __TEXT_EXEC. xnu-12377.121.x (26.5) gained the matching case in
osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c (`segTEXTEXECB != segKCTEXTEXECB`). Older kernels
only know the previous layout: they compute the kext text range as "the KC's
__TEXT_EXEC after the kernel's __LAST", get zero for it, and panic in
arm_vm_init() with

    Assertion failed: segSizePLKDATACONST && segSizePLKTEXTEXEC

before the console is up (macOS 26.3's KDK kernels, for example).

dyld-1340 (26.3's dyld, and so 26.3's kmutil) had no partition and laid the
kernel's text out first. This hunk makes that order selectable through the
environment -- KCB_TEXT_EXEC_ORDER=kernel-first -- and leaves the default
(kexts first) as kmutil has it. bench-kc-build sets it from --text-exec-order.

diff --git a/kernel-collection-builder/AppCacheBuilder.cpp b/kernel-collection-builder/AppCacheBuilder.cpp
index f31906f..814878e 100644
--- a/kernel-collection-builder/AppCacheBuilder.cpp
+++ b/kernel-collection-builder/AppCacheBuilder.cpp
@@ -478,11 +478,21 @@ void AppCacheBuilder::assignSegmentRegionsAndOffsets()
         for ( AppCacheDylibInfo& dylib : sortedDylibs ) {
             textSortedDylibs.push_back(&dylib);
         }
-        std::stable_partition(textSortedDylibs.begin(), textSortedDylibs.end(), [](const AppCacheDylibInfo* a) {
-            // Sort static exe last, kexts first
-            const UnsafeHeader* hdr = (const UnsafeHeader*)a->input->mappedFile.mh;
-            return hdr->isKextBundle();
-        });
+        // KCB_TEXT_EXEC_ORDER=kernel-first keeps the pre-dyld-1378 order (the
+        // kernel's __TEXT_EXEC first, the kexts' after its __LAST), which is the
+        // only layout xnu <= 12377.81.x (macOS 26.3) accepts: its arm_vm_init()
+        // derives the kext text range as "KC __TEXT_EXEC after the kernel's
+        // __LAST" and asserts (segSizePLKDATACONST && segSizePLKTEXTEXEC) when
+        // that range is empty. xnu 12377.121.x (26.5) added the kexts-first case.
+        const char* textExecOrder = getenv("KCB_TEXT_EXEC_ORDER");
+        bool kernelTextExecFirst = (textExecOrder != nullptr) && (strcmp(textExecOrder, "kernel-first") == 0);
+        if ( !kernelTextExecFirst ) {
+            std::stable_partition(textSortedDylibs.begin(), textSortedDylibs.end(), [](const AppCacheDylibInfo* a) {
+                // Sort static exe last, kexts first
+                const UnsafeHeader* hdr = (const UnsafeHeader*)a->input->mappedFile.mh;
+                return hdr->isKextBundle();
+            });
+        }
 
         __block uint64_t offsetInRegion = 0;
         for ( AppCacheDylibInfo* dylib : textSortedDylibs ) {
